    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 3.625,
      "text": "Most losing poker hands are born before the flop."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.625,
      "end": 11.125,
      "text": "Queen-seven offsuit looks playable because it has a face card, but a face card does not mean profitable."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.125,
      "end": 16.125,
      "text": "This hand makes weak pairs, bad kickers, and dominated trouble."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.125,
      "end": 21.625,
      "text": "Good starting hands can make strong pairs, strong draws, or nutted hands."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.625,
      "end": 26.5,
      "text": "Bad starting hands make second-best hands that cost you chips later."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.5,
      "end": 29.916666666666668,
      "text": "The cleanest fix is discipline before the flop."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.916666666666668,
      "end": 33.875,
      "text": "You do not need to outplay a mistake you never enter."
    }
  ],
